<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the Developer ID signature
  (tools/package-macos.sh with MITCAD_SIGN_IDENTITY; ad-hoc builds use none).

  Mitcad needs no exception from the hardened runtime: it has no JIT and
  writes no executable memory (com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit is absent),
  loads no unsigned or third-party plug-ins, and OpenGL needs no
  entitlement. com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation is absent on
  purpose: every dylib, framework and Qt plug-in in the bundle (Qt, OCCT,
  FreeType) is signed with the same Developer ID as the application, so
  library validation passes and stays on, which keeps a foreign dylib from
  being injected. Add it only if a component that is signed by someone else
  is ever loaded, and note the reason here.

  The app is not sandboxed (it opens files anywhere and starts its own
  executable for the .f3d import worker), so there is no
  com.apple.security.app-sandbox either.
-->
